<title>LEBANON: All Lebanese t-bill yields fall.</title>
<headline>All Lebanese t-bill yields fall.</headline>
<dateline>BEIRUT 1996-12-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>All yields fell on Lebanese treasury bills, according to weekly rates issued by the Bank of Lebanon on Monday.</p>
<p>It announced the following interest rates for its December 5 issues (previous week in brackets):</p>
<p>    Term		     Discount		     Yield</p>
<p>				(percent)		   (percent)</p>
<p>    Three months	  13.86 (13.89)	     14.36 (14.39)</p>
<p>    Six months	    15.23 (15.29)	     16.48 (16.55)</p>
<p>    12 months	     14.90 (14.95)	     17.50 (17.57)</p>
<p>    24 months   (Interest payable twice yearly) 20.76 (21.00)</p>
<p>-Beirut editorial (961 1) 864148 602057 645456</p>
